Close the File-Manager window when it opens a file.

xwpe already supports this via the FM_CLOSE_WINDOW option flag: when set, the
open path in WpeHandleFileManager calls e_close_window(f) before e_edit().
The flag is just off by default, so picking a file leaves the File-Manager
window sitting behind the new editor. Enable it in the default flopt so
opening a file from the File-Manager dismisses the manager, matching the
expectation that the editor takes over. Users can still toggle it back off
in the File-Manager options dialog.

--- a/we_main.c
+++ b/we_main.c
@@ -325,7 +325,7 @@
  cn->tabs = MALLOC((cn->tabn+1)*sizeof(char));
  WpeStringBlank(cn->tabs, cn->tabn);
  cn->flopt = FM_REKURSIVE_ACTIONS | FM_REMOVE_INTO_WB | FM_MOVE_PROMPT |
-   FM_MOVE_PROMPT | FM_PROMPT_DELETE;
+   FM_MOVE_PROMPT | FM_PROMPT_DELETE | FM_CLOSE_WINDOW;
  cn->edopt = ED_SOURCE_AUTO_INDENT | ED_ERRORS_STOP_AT | ED_SYNTAX_HIGHLIGHT;
 }
 
